laurel 2201: Mi A3 AMOLED brightness and panel power: panel from the INTF_1 timing, DCS max 2047 (Samsung s6e8fco) / 4095 (GVO r692a9), AppleARMBacklight only with the GPU renderer (apollo 0154 slider protocol), fades (apollo 0151). The Mi A3 has two AMOLEDs (laurel_sprout-trinket-display.dtsi): Samsung bl-max 2047, GVO bl-max 4095, both min 4, default 268, DCS 0x51 MSB first (F9S dsi_panel_set_brightness), 0x53 0x20 brightness control on; off-command delays Samsung 0x28 20 ms / 0x10 120 ms, GVO 50 / 20 ms (unknown 50 / 120). ABL/Mu leave the video timing in INTF_1 HSYNC_CTL: htotal 1404 / pulse 40 = Samsung, 1360 / 136 = GVO; unknown = Samsung range. Self-check at start: the DT default level through the DSI command DMA; no DONE = feature off (display off keeps the black frame). AppleARMBacklight (topaz 0105; topaz 0110 made it opt-in because CoreBrightness's digital dimming took the CPU renderer under 1 fps) is published by a thread only after RedwoodGPU appears (TopazAdreno.cpp publishes it when the Adreno runs; wait 180 s), else CoreBrightness keeps IOMFBBrightnessLevel. It publishes IODisplayParameters brightness {0, 255, value} + brightness-nits + max-nits 430 (estimate, no source value) and takes {brightness, FadePeriod} (DBV = max * (v/255)^2); once that slider is used, IOMFBBrightnessLevel is ignored (first use of each is logged). The level is at least 4 while the display is on. blWork walks to a new level in 16 ms steps over the fade time. Power changes are serialized (fPwrLock) and hold blWork off: display off = fade the light out over 300 ms while frames still show, then fPowerOff (black kernel frame), 0x28/0x10 with the panel's delays; on = fPowerOff clear, 0x11, 120 ms, 0x29, 0x53 0x20, one frame (one retry; twice not done = feature off with one line), then fade in to the last level. dsiSend sets COMMAND_MODE_DMA_CTRL bit 28 (embedded mode) as Linux does. Lines: `LAUREL BACKLIGHT: on: DCS max N (<panel>: INTF1 hsync 0x...), level 268, 430 nits (estimate